[B]PackMerger 1.3.0[/B] - every player gets the pack, every time

This release fixes the delivery and hosting problems that made players play without the pack, triples the number of plugins whose packs are picked up automatically, merges 1.21.4+ item definitions correctly, and adds a plugin API, a fix-up command for other pack hosts and a BungeeCord proxy plugin.

[B]Fixed[/B]
[LIST]
[*][B]Returning players got no pack.[/B] The player cache skipped the send on rejoin, but the client drops server packs on disconnect. The pack is now sent on every join; the client's own SHA-1 cache avoids re-downloading.
[*][B]Every merge looked like a new pack.[/B] Zip timestamps made identical content hash differently. Merged and staged zips are now deterministic.
[*][B]Hash/URL mismatch window.[/B] URL, SHA-1 and pack id are published together, only after the upload succeeded. A failed upload keeps the previous pack live.
[*][B]No pack after a restart or /pm reload[/B] until a merge finished. The last merged pack is republished immediately; self-host no longer answers 503 after a reload.
[*][B]Players who joined before the first merge[/B] now get it as soon as it is published; failed downloads are resent automatically (capped), and the status handling only reacts to PackMerger's own pack.
[*][B]Pack stacking and stripping.[/B] One stable pack id per server; PackMerger removes only its own previous pack instead of clearing packs sent by a proxy or other plugins.
[*][B]Self-host advertised localhost on most servers.[/B] The host is resolved from [FONT=Courier New]public-url[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]public-host[/FONT], an opt-in public IP lookup, [FONT=Courier New]server-ip[/FONT] and the bind address; a non-routable result is loudly warned about and explained in [FONT=Courier New]/pm status[/FONT]. The HTTP handler now matches exact paths and supports HEAD, ETag/304 and Range.
[*][B]1.21.4+ item definitions[/B] from two packs are unioned instead of the lower-priority one being dropped; overlay folders get the same merge rules as [FONT=Courier New]assets/[/FONT]; legacy overrides are sorted by CustomModelData; hot reload sees edits inside pack folders.
[*][B]Plugin packs:[/B] corrected EliteMobs and FreeMinecraftModels paths, broken Nexo/ItemsAdder/Oraxen fallbacks removed, stale staged packs deleted, half-written zips never staged.
[*][B]The plugin API and events were invisible to other plugins[/B] (isolated classloader). They can be used now.
[/LIST]

[B]Added[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Download verification after every upload, [FONT=Courier New]upload.fallback[/FONT] providers, [FONT=Courier New]public-host[/FONT], opt-in [FONT=Courier New]detect-public-ip[/FONT], port and rcon/query collision warnings, admin join notices when hosting looks broken.
[*][FONT=Courier New]distribution.retry[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]distribution.enforce-required[/FONT] (off by default: kick on decline or after failed retries), [FONT=Courier New]distribution.skip-bedrock-players[/FONT].
[*]13 more plugin-pack integrations (Nova, BetterHUD, ValhallaMMO, vane-core, BackpackPlus, BetterStructures, CannonRTP, EternalTD, InfiniteVehicles, MegaBlockSurvivors, ResurrectionChest, MMOInventory, RealisticSurvival), cluster folders, operator-defined adapters, a watcher that re-merges when a plugin rebuilds its pack, and [FONT=Courier New]/pm merge[/FONT].
[*][FONT=Courier New]merge.model-policy[/FONT], merge notes in [FONT=Courier New]/pm inspect[/FONT], overlay format repair.
[*]Pack registration API ([FONT=Courier New]PackMergerApi.registerPack[/FONT]) and [FONT=Courier New]PackMergerCollectPacksEvent[/FONT].
[*]Detection of ItemsAdder, Oraxen and Nexo hosting their own pack, with [FONT=Courier New]/pm fixup <plugin>[/FONT] to back up and fix their config.
[*][FONT=Courier New]/pm verbose[/FONT], a much richer [FONT=Courier New]/pm status[/FONT], [FONT=Courier New]merge.output-copy-to[/FONT], Geyser folder auto-detection, Bedrock manifest versions that follow the content.
[*]BungeeCord proxy plugin, HMAC-signed proxy messages ([FONT=Courier New]distribution.proxy-secret[/FONT]), persisted proxy state, network or per-server proxy modes.
[/LIST]

[B]Changed - read before updating[/B]
[LIST]
[*]Paper 26.3 support: the pack-format check knows 26.3 (format 97). The jar is compiled against the 26.1.2 API on purpose (Paper 26.3 ships Adventure 5; a jar built against it would crash on 26.1/26.2) and tested on 26.3, so one jar runs on 26.1, 26.2 and 26.3.
[*]Update the Velocity/Bungee proxy plugin together with the backends: the proxy message format is now v2.
[*][FONT=Courier New]upload.self-host.port[/FONT] defaults to Minecraft port + 1 for configs without the key (existing explicit ports are kept).
[*][FONT=Courier New]public-url[/FONT] is now a complete URL; [FONT=Courier New]/pack[/FONT] is only appended when the URL has no path.
[*][FONT=Courier New]distribution.cache[/FONT] is gone (ignored if present). Replace mode no longer clears other plugins' packs.
[*]Default model/blockstate merge is whole-file; set [FONT=Courier New]merge.model-policy: deep[/FONT] for the old behaviour.
[*]The plugin-pack watcher is on by default. Config version is now 6; old configs keep working.
[/LIST]

Full changelog: [URL='https://github.com/PCX-Network/PackMerger/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md']CHANGELOG.md[/URL]
